tline support agents. Thus for what should have been a clear and straightforward fault, which Coinbase ought to have corrected on the spot and with an apology, instead became a wasted 2 hours of my time where the support agent offered no apology, no remedy, and frankly nothing but an incoherent mix of standard pasted Coinbase support agent phrases and a complete lack of understanding on the part of the agent. Not enough that Coinbase and its platform clearly failed the agreement that my funds would be automatically unlocked after 5 days, but it then also added insult and further injury by wilfully and completely wasting XXXX hours of my time without any remedy, follow-up, or outcome. it is now another 5 days later, XX/XX/XXXX, and still even today my fund balance remains locked and not available to send or withdraw ( see screenshot XXXX ). Again, this kind problem, both in terms of the initial core failure and the subsequent failure of support and rectification, is sadly not just an isolated issue, but is recurring continuously. In effect, Coinbase is taking advantage of retail customers, just because it seems to think it can, and because Coinbase knows that for instance holding many customer funds improperly locked for longer than agreed will cumulatively increase profits for Coinbase. This kind of tactic may be lucrative and thus understandable, but it is nonetheless improper, and totally unbefitting for a reputable financial institution. Yet Coinbase keep on with its improprieties as though it was licensed to take advantage of customers without any accountability for its problems. Personally I am fed up with this and I refuse to keep being victimised by Coinbase conduct, hence I am starting to defend myself here. Again, if Coinbase wants to operate as a financial institution in the XXXX, it needs to start acting as a financial institution rather than as a shady platform specialized in profiteering from customers without any accountability.",,"Coinbase, Inc.",CA,9