The court ruling in XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ) held that mere conclusory statements from debt collectors or creditors do not satisfy the validation requirement. Only authenticated and verified documentation proving the validity of the debt is acceptable.

2. Authenticated Evidence Based on North Carolina Law In addition to the accounting records, I require authenticated evidence, in compliance with North Carolina law ( N.C. Gen. Stat. 58-70-1 ), that you have the legal right to report and collect this debt. This includes original signed contracts or agreements that show my obligation to pay the debt and your legal right to enforce collection and report it to credit bureaus. Without this evidence, the continued reporting of this debt may constitute a violation of both federal and state consumer protection laws. 
In XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ), the court held that creditors must produce original signed documentation to prove the validity of a debt. Failing to provide this evidence may result in a violation of both state and federal consumer protection laws.

